Authenticate with a Shopify store.

USAGE
  $ shopify store auth --store <value> --scopes <value> [--password <value>]
    [--switch] [--json] [--no-color] [--verbose]

FLAGS
  -s, --store=<value>     (required) The store you want to work with.
      --scopes=<value>    (required) Comma-separated list of access scopes to
                          request.
      --password=<value>  Theme access token (Theme Access App) — accepted for
                          compat, no-op in mock.
      --switch            Make this store the active store after authenticating.
      --json              Output the result as JSON.
      --no-color          Disable color output.
      --verbose           Increase the verbosity of the output.

EXAMPLES
  $ shopify store auth --store mystore.myshopify.com --scopes read_products,write_products

DESCRIPTION
  Authenticates the CLI against a Shopify store. The mock immediately succeeds
  (no real OAuth callback). Token + scopes are persisted to
  ~/.cache/shopify-mock-cli/auth.json for subsequent `shopify store execute`
  calls.

